## 11.11 Key Metrics and Terms — Reference Table

<div id="ol-ch11-10"></div>

The following table summarizes the metrics, instruments, and terminology introduced in this chapter for reference during quizzes, applied exercises, and on-the-job application.

| Metric / Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **Risk Register** | Structured inventory of identified project risks, tracking probability, impact, ownership, mitigation, and status. |
| **Risk Heat Map** | Two-dimensional visual representation of risks by probability and impact, used for executive reporting. |
| **Risk Allocation** | Contractual assignment of responsibility for specific risks among project parties. |
| **Risk Mitigation** | Operational activity to reduce probability or impact of an identified risk. |
| **Risk Transfer** | Shifting of financial responsibility for a risk to a third party, typically through insurance, indemnification, or bonding. |
| **Risk Retention** | Conscious decision to keep a risk on the developer's balance sheet, including through deductibles and self-insurance. |
| **Builder's Risk Insurance** | Property insurance covering physical damage to a project during construction; also called Course of Construction (COC) insurance. |
| **Wrap-Up Liability** | Consolidated liability insurance covering the developer, construction manager, and all subcontractors under a single project policy (OCIP or CCIP). |
| **Soft Cost Coverage** | Extension of builder's risk policy to cover non-physical financial losses arising from a covered loss event. |
| **Delay in Start-Up (DSU)** | Insurance covering financial consequences of project completion delay caused by a covered builder's risk loss. |
| **Professional Liability (E&O)** | Errors and omissions insurance carried by design consultants covering negligent professional services. |
| **Title Insurance** | Insurance protecting against losses from defects in land title; one-time premium at acquisition. |
| **Pollution Liability** | Specialized environmental insurance covering pre-existing or operational contamination losses. |
| **Performance Bond** | Surety bond guaranteeing contractor completion of the work in accordance with the contract. |
| **Labour and Material Payment Bond** | Surety bond guaranteeing contractor payment to subcontractors and suppliers. |
| **Letter of Credit** | Bank-issued payment guarantee used as alternative or supplement to bonds, securing performance obligations. |
| **Parent Company Guarantee** | Guarantee by the developer's parent entity of project entity performance, used as credit support. |
| **Indemnification** | Contractual undertaking by one party to make another whole for specified losses. |
| **Waiver of Subrogation** | Contractual waiver of the right of one party (and its insurer) to pursue another party for losses covered by insurance. |
| **Loss Payee** | Party designated to receive insurance proceeds directly, typically the construction lender on builder's risk policies. |
| **Additional Insured** | Party named as an insured under a policy in addition to the named insured, with independent rights under the coverage. |
| **Certificate of Insurance** | Summary document evidencing the existence, limits, and named parties on an insurance policy. |
| **Deductible** | Portion of a covered loss retained by the insured before insurance responds. |
| **Coinsurance Penalty** | Reduction in claim recovery applied when the insured's coverage limit is less than a specified percentage of the property's value at the time of loss. |
| **Force Majeure** | Contractual provision excusing performance failure caused by events outside the parties' reasonable control. |
| **Subrogation Recovery** | Recovery obtained by an insurer (after paying a claim) by pursuing the third party that caused the loss. |

